<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6148"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 1:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Q <BR> <BR>I hadn´t notice the HAPPy Clown , don´t know if it has anything to do with the HAPP KAKEMANN though. <BR>Another thing, try comparing the dark comlexed BTK sketch with the dark haired, mustach guy with star-shirt, from A Blackout, He is in the same link as the Happy Clown. <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
