<!--Post: 6189--><!--Time: 1107569915-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Lilymarie <BR> <BR>Tom deleeted it, here it is. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html" target=_top>http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html</a> <BR> <BR>And TOM this IS related to the Vian case because the neighbour of Vian who possibly was the original intended victim used to go to this &#34;A Blackout&#34; you can read about it in the newsreport that I posted as#1 on this thred. <BR> <BR>thank you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6189-->
<!--Post: 6195--><!--Time: 1107571939-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6195"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh, Gil McNabb. I researched him a couple of months ago - but I was more focused on Tom Bevan &#40;photographer&#41; because he took many of the photos of the Beats and A Blackout Tavern. I can&#39;t remember why I discounted McNabb...and I couldn&#39;t find Bevan - except for a guy on a &#34;RealPolitics&#34; website that looked like it was sponsered by Fox or something. <BR> <BR>BUT - now that you mention the resemblence...hmmm<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6195-->
<!--Post: 6069--><!--Time: 1107520398-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting story...I really wonder if his victims were really that random based on oppurtunity...He couldnt get who he wanted so he just killed someone close? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6069-->
<!--Post: 6079--><!--Time: 1107528156-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;She still wonders why the first investigators didn&#39;t bring Vian&#39;s son to see her, to see whether she and her son were the same people in the picture.&#34; <BR> <BR>Yes, why not? <BR> <BR>Marga <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6079-->
<!--Post: 6145--><!--Time: 1107551049-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6145"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Salem<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Salem<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 1:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think it is interesting though that he knew there was a woman living, as the article notes, &#34;three doors down.&#34; Wonder why he wouldn&#39;t just go next door?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6145-->
<!--Post: 6153--><!--Time: 1107553694-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 1:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK was in the process of trying to locate his &#34;intended&#34; victim when Vian&#39;s son walked by. Thinking it could be the boy in the picture, BTK stopped him to take a better look at him. He noticed the Vian son was not the one in the pic but noticed which house he entered. When nobody answered BTK&#39;s knock at the first place he went to the Vian house.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6153-->
<!--Post: 6167--><!--Time: 1107562739-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6167"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitagirl31<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitagirl31<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My theory is with MSrusty, it is very interesting. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6167-->
<!--Post: 6169--><!--Time: 1107564190-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6169"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was planning to post that I disagree with this theory because BTK put too much effort &amp; pride into planning and stalking to just decide on a whim to change victims. <BR> <BR>Then I remebered a post in &#34;From BTK&#34; stating &#34;it had been a spur of the moment trasaction&#34;. Do the streets referred to in this post coincide with the Vian location? <BR> <BR>For the record, to this point, I have not believed the posts were actually from BTK. If this is accurate I may change my opimion. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6169-->
<!--Post: 6198--><!--Time: 1107573489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6198"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 7:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I do think he stalked his victims, but in this case he maybe was hyped up about a killing and when the first door wasn&#39;t answered, he went on to the Vian house. This might also explain an earlier post I read about phone lines being cut. Vian&#39;s was not cut, this could be why. Also Wegerle&#39;s was not cut, and I thought I read in one of letters that this one was a spur of the moment killing. This is only my opinion of course.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6198-->
<!--Post: 6278--><!--Time: 1107654224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6278"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 5:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is my take on this for all it&#39;s worth. I do not think Cheryl was an intended victim. <BR> <BR>Remember, a 5 year old boy saw a man knocking on her door but she was not home. A lot of people are speculating that the man the child saw is the same man. Could be, but doesn&#39;t mean it is.  <BR> <BR>He had a picture of Shirley Vian and her son for Christ sakes. He knew exactly who he was going after and had most likely been in her home prior to the murder. Welcomed or not, who knows right now other than BTK himself.  <BR> <BR>I say he was most likely in her home prior to the murder because the photo was not a new photo, Steve was only a baby in the photo and he was 5 when his mother&#39;s murder took place. Where else would BTK have gotten this photo other than her house? The only other thing I can think of is in stalking her, at some point lifted it straight out of her purse, and then preceded to find her at her residence. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6278-->
<!--Post: 6279--><!--Time: 1107654486-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6279"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Berkeley_street<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Berkeley_street<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 5:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It was the Wegerle&#39;s murder that was a spur of the moment thing. He also said that it was his favorite or something to that affect. Because it wasn&#39;t planned and it was &#34;a spur of the moment transaction&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6279-->
<!--Post: 6280--><!--Time: 1107654657-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 5:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Berkeley_Street-I am not refering to the wegerle murder. This woman Cheryl claims that she may have been an intended victim of BTK instead of Shirley Vian because a 5 year old boy saw a man knocking on her door the same day that Shirley Vian was murdered.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6280-->
<!--Post: 6281--><!--Time: 1107654731-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Berkeley_street<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Berkeley_street<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was under the impression that they had stated that the photo he showed the little boy was not Shirley Vian and her son. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
