<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6322"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->March 17, 1977 <BR> <BR>Shirley Vians 6yr old son is shown photo of woman and child, who he didn&#39;t recognize, by strange man. <BR>&#40;her son had been at Dillons getting a money order&#41; <BR> <BR>Apx 11:45 the same man shows up at the door &#40;with briefcase or bowling bag&#41; and the 6yr old &#40;recent story says 5yr old&#41;opened it, and when asked, said his mom was sick in bed. <BR> <BR>Man forces his way in with gun and Shirley hears noise and gets up.  <BR> <BR>There are three kids present who were locked in bathroom: <BR> <BR>6yr old boy. Was the boy that was shown the picture of an unidentified woman and child. The man asked if he recognized them. He didn&#39;t. He is the same boy who answered the door when the same man reappeared and entered. This was the same boy who was recently interviewed and said that he looked through the top of the door and could see the man murdering his mother. <BR> <BR>8yr old boy. He was bound at the hands before being locked in the bathroom. <BR> <BR>4yr old girl. Was locked in the bathroom. In BTK&#39;s letter in reference to the murder, he expressed regret that he was spooked by the phone and didn&#39;t have time to hang her.  <BR> <BR>Of all BTK&#39;s correspondence, the most notable aspect that I&#39;ve found is his inconsistant attitude toward girls. He seems to target grown women, yet the treatment of the Josephine Otero, and his reference to Shirley Vian&#39;s daughter seem to point to a very strong sexual preference for young girls. It might be that he does not even consciously realize it or can&#39;t conciously cope with it. That would make it a weakness that can be exploited or will trip him up. I bet there is an achilles heel there somewhere.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6322-->
<!--Post: 6882--><!--Time: 1108061932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6882"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 10:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->im wondering if maybe BTK knows Cheryl &#40;well&#41;and had been to her house before. Maybe even enough to target Shirley.  Maybe he asked Shirley&#39;s boy if knew Cheryl, and her boy, to determine whether he had to kill him for fear that he may provide a description that clicked with Cheryl. Similarly,  he may have wanted to make sure Cheryl wasnt home when he went for his true target &#40;Shirley&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
